From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 14:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: Force full PSP hw_init on runtime resume

During D3cold runtime power-cycling (e.g. via Apple GMUX PWRD(1)), VRAM
power is completely cut, causing the PSP to lose its internal state,
loaded firmware (SOS), and Trusted Memory Region (TMR)[cite: 1, 2].

Standard psp_resume() only executes psp_hw_start(), assuming the PSP
state and TMR remained intact during suspend[cite: 1]. This results in command
timeouts ("PSP load kdb failed!", error -62) when waking up from D3cold.

Reset psp->initialized to false and invoke psp_hw_init() during runtime
PM (adev->in_runpm) to force a full firmware reload, TMR reconstruction,
and ring initialization [Quelle: drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_psp.c].

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_psp.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_psp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_psp.c
index 9bd6b2a8d4e2..f0a41d9c12b1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_psp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_psp.c
@@ -3351,6 +3351,9 @@ static int psp_resume(struct amdgpu_ip_block *ip_block)
 	struct amdgpu_device *adev = ip_block->adev;
 	struct psp_context *psp = &adev->psp;

+	if (adev->in_runpm)
+		return psp_hw_init(ip_block);
+
 	ret = psp_hw_start(psp);
 	if (ret)
 		goto failed;
-- 
